### Methods: Diagnostic Accuracy (STARD 2015 Compliant)

Diagnostic test accuracy of {{ index_test | default("the index test") }} was evaluated against {{ reference_standard | default("the reference standard") }} in {{ n_total | default(0) }} enrolled patients. True positive (TP), false positive (FP), false negative (FN), and true negative (TN) counts were extracted into standard 2x2 contingency tables.

Diagnostic accuracy parameters including Sensitivity, Specificity, Positive Likelihood Ratio (+LR), Negative Likelihood Ratio (-LR), and Diagnostic Odds Ratio (DOR) were calculated with exact binomial 95% confidence intervals (Wilson score intervals). Receiver Operating Characteristic (ROC) curves were constructed, and the Area Under the Curve (AUC-ROC) was calculated via trapezoidal integration with DeLong 95% CIs. Clinical utility and post-test disease probabilities were modeled using Fagan nomograms across low, moderate, and high pre-test probability clinical scenarios.
